From: mayipashu <mayipashu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 06:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fmcs: compare only the GPON control bits this function owns

set_gpon_downstream() does a read-modify-write of FPGA register
0x01000004 and requires the read-back to equal the written value
exactly. That register has bits the FMCS FPGA drives by itself while the
downstream PON engine is running, so the read-back intermittently returns
0x3 for a written 0x2 and the function reports

    GPON control readback mismatch: wanted 0x00000002, got 0x00000003

The caller (h3c_hm2004_du/runtime.rs) turns that into fail_closed(): the
optical owner is pinned in OpticalState::Unknown, the laser is turned off
and only an explicit reload recovers. On H3C HM2004-DU this is visible as
the downstream port dying mid-session ("optical state is unconfirmed;
transmission recovery attempted; explicit reload required") and taking
the connected ONUs offline with it.

Restrict both the write decision and the verification to the bits this
function owns (TX and FEC). Genuine faults on those bits are still
reported; hardware-owned status bits are left alone, which also avoids
writing a status/W1C bit back.

Observed on H3C HM2004-DU with the 2026-11-24 build: the port came up
after a reload (register 0x2, TX on, diagnostics valid: 44 C, 3.31 V,
16.81 mA, -1.04 dBm) and dropped again 28 s later with that mismatch.
--- a/fttr/src/src/platform/h3c_hm2004_du/fmcs.rs
+++ b/fttr/src/src/platform/h3c_hm2004_du/fmcs.rs
@@ -161,14 +161,21 @@
     mut write: impl FnMut(u32) -> io::Result<()>,
 ) -> io::Result<u32> {
     let before = read()?;
-    let target = (before & !(GPON_TX | GPON_FEC))
-        | if tx { GPON_TX } else { 0 }
-        | if fec { GPON_FEC } else { 0 };
-    if before != target {
+    /*
+     * Owned bits only. The FMCS FPGA drives other bits of this register
+     * itself while the downstream PON engine is running, so both the
+     * "needs a write" decision and the read-back check must ignore them:
+     * a strict comparison fails at random, the caller runs fail_closed()
+     * and the optical port stays disabled until fttrd is reloaded, which
+     * on this board shows up as the line dropping mid-session.
+     */
+    let owned = GPON_TX | GPON_FEC;
+    let target = (before & !owned) | if tx { GPON_TX } else { 0 } | if fec { GPON_FEC } else { 0 };
+    if before & owned != target & owned {
         write(target)?;
     }
     let actual = read()?;
-    if actual != target {
+    if actual & owned != target & owned {
         return Err(io::Error::other(format!(
             "GPON control readback mismatch: wanted {target:#010x}, got {actual:#010x}"
         )));
